!id: Y66TinmI3l
!text:
\[
{{c2::e::\ldots}}
=
\lim_{n \to \infty} {{c1::\left( 1 + \frac{1}{n} \right)^n::\ldots}}
\]
~~~

!id: s3DJR4PMXP
!text:
\[
{{c2::e^x::\ldots}}
=
\lim_{n \to \infty} {{c1::\left( 1 + \frac{x}{n} \right)^n::\ldots}}
\]
~~~

!id: ctqWbhBToB
!text:
\[
{{c2::e::\ldots}}
=
\lim_{h \to 0} {{c1::\left( 1 + h \right)^{1 / h}::\ldots}}
\]
~~~

!id: kH3ZZfYUe1
!text:
\[
{{c2::e^x::\ldots}}
=
\lim_{h \to 0} {{c1::\left( 1 + h \right)^{x / h}::\ldots}}
\]
~~~

!id: xccjUZGTRa
!text:
\[
{{c2::\ln a::\ldots}}
=
{{c1::\lim_{x \to 0} \frac{a^x - 1}{x}::\lim_{x \to \ldots} \ldots}}, \quad a > 0
\]
~~~

!id: 4gyUssEC4i
!text:
\[
\lim_{n \to \infty} n^{1/n}
=
{{c1::1::\ldots}}
\]
!back extra:
Write \( n^{1/n} = e^{\ln n / n} \). By L'Hôpital's rule applied to \( \ln x / x \) as \( x \to \infty \),
\[ \lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{\ln x}{x} = \lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{1/x}{1} = 0, \]
and since \( \exp \) is continuous,
\[ n^{1/n} = e^{\ln n / n} \to e^0 = 1. \]
~~~

!id: hHI7p525Ms
!text: \[ \lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{x^n}{e^x} = {{c1::0::\ldots}} \]
~~~

!id: HoJDXwwlgd
!text: \[ \lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{\ln x}{x^a} = {{c1::0::\ldots}}, \quad a > 0 \]
~~~

!id: AIxLlhWerJ
!text: \[ \lim_{n \to \infty} \frac{x^n}{n!} = {{c1::0::\ldots}} \]
~~~
